––– comment –––
Regression for #5008: expression filters on right-table attributes must be evaluated on the right side for INNER JOIN and after the join for LEFT JOIN.
––– block: ../base/start-searchd –––
––– input –––
mysql -h0 -P9306 -e "DROP TABLE IF EXISTS gh5008_chunks; DROP TABLE IF EXISTS gh5008_docs; CREATE TABLE gh5008_docs (path string attribute); CREATE TABLE gh5008_chunks (content text, doc_id bigint); INSERT INTO gh5008_docs (id,path) VALUES (1,'c:/Borges/a.txt'),(2,'gh5008_docs.path'),(300,'c:/borges/c.txt'),(400,'c:/other/path.txt'); INSERT INTO gh5008_chunks (id,content,doc_id) VALUES (1,'one two three',1),(2,'one two',2),(3,'one two four',300),(4,'one two five',400),(5,'one two six',999);"
––– output –––
––– comment –––
Filter the right table using a REGEX expression (the original report).
––– input –––
mysql --skip-table --batch --raw --skip-column-names -h0 -P9306 -e "SELECT gh5008_chunks.id FROM gh5008_chunks INNER JOIN gh5008_docs ON gh5008_chunks.doc_id=gh5008_docs.id WHERE MATCH('@content \"one two\"') AND REGEX(gh5008_docs.path, '(?i)borges') ORDER BY id ASC;"
––– output –––
1
3
––– comment –––
Both a right-table expression filter and a regular right-table filter.
––– input –––
mysql --skip-table --batch --raw --skip-column-names -h0 -P9306 -e "SELECT gh5008_chunks.id FROM gh5008_chunks INNER JOIN gh5008_docs ON gh5008_chunks.doc_id=gh5008_docs.id WHERE REGEX(gh5008_docs.path, '(?i)borges') AND gh5008_docs.id>100 ORDER BY id ASC;"
––– output –––
3
––– comment –––
The regex pattern is a literal: do not strip table names from its contents.
––– input –––
mysql --skip-table --batch --raw --skip-column-names -h0 -P9306 -e "SELECT gh5008_chunks.id FROM gh5008_chunks INNER JOIN gh5008_docs ON gh5008_chunks.doc_id=gh5008_docs.id WHERE REGEX(gh5008_docs.path, 'gh5008_docs.path') ORDER BY id ASC;"
––– output –––
2
––– comment –––
Negated right-table expression filter.
––– input –––
mysql --skip-table --batch --raw --skip-column-names -h0 -P9306 -e "SELECT gh5008_chunks.id FROM gh5008_chunks INNER JOIN gh5008_docs ON gh5008_chunks.doc_id=gh5008_docs.id WHERE NOT REGEX(gh5008_docs.path, '(?i)borges') ORDER BY id ASC;"
––– output –––
2
4
––– comment –––
LEFT JOIN must fetch the right-hand attribute even though only the left id is selected.
––– input –––
mysql --skip-table --batch --raw --skip-column-names -h0 -P9306 -e "SELECT gh5008_chunks.id FROM gh5008_chunks LEFT JOIN gh5008_docs ON gh5008_chunks.doc_id=gh5008_docs.id WHERE REGEX(gh5008_docs.path, '(?i)borges') ORDER BY id ASC;"
––– output –––
1
3
––– comment –––
Mixed filter trees must be evaluated after LEFT JOIN, including unmatched left rows.
––– input –––
mysql --skip-table --batch --raw --skip-column-names -h0 -P9306 -e "SELECT gh5008_chunks.id FROM gh5008_chunks LEFT JOIN gh5008_docs ON gh5008_chunks.doc_id=gh5008_docs.id WHERE REGEX(gh5008_docs.path, '(?i)borges') OR gh5008_chunks.doc_id=999 ORDER BY id ASC;"
––– output –––
1
3
5
––– comment –––
The same results with join batching disabled.
––– input –––
mysql --skip-table --batch --raw --skip-column-names -h0 -P9306 -e "SELECT gh5008_chunks.id FROM gh5008_chunks INNER JOIN gh5008_docs ON gh5008_chunks.doc_id=gh5008_docs.id WHERE REGEX(gh5008_docs.path, '(?i)borges') ORDER BY id ASC OPTION join_batch_size=0;"
––– output –––
1
3
